There are better solutions....take the game I had last night for instance...
Wizard, lvl 3, desends into level 4.  Suddenly, I notice a large reduction
in the speed of the game (unacc. Amiga), and I figured, hey there must be
5 or more creatures present already.  After a while I hear crashing rock,
and one of the wall spaces in a nearby room disappears.  Figuring that a 
drawf was nearby, I walked into the room....no drawf, but 5 Killer Bees, and
TWO wall spaces were gone now.  Bees made a B-line for me (no pun int.), and
so did 2 ghosts from my previous characters.  Only chance was to try inventory.
I put on an unidentified ring and suddenly:
the killer bee misses masem's ghost -more-
the killer bee misses the killer bee -more-
..
and several more messages of that type.  Well, after several free attacks
on monsters, the results of 2 scrolls of monster summoning, the dwarf, and
a THRID ghost, I was up against 1 killer bee, which promply fell.  Collected
all the loot, found the ex-equipment of the previous characters, visited a
store above, and uncursed/blesses all usable equipment.  So back on level
4, ready to descend, when
The orc hits! -more-
The orc hits! -more-
You die... -more-

*sigh*.  Cant wait to get to that bones level....
